From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emuTOS-MCD <darekadumon@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 20:45:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 061/184] segacd: hold the head after a read instead of letting
 it run to the rim

Command 3 does not read a sector, it starts the drive reading, and the
drive keeps going. Nothing stopped it between one read and the next, so
across a request -- across GEMDOS -- it ran forward to the end of the
disc and sat in the lead-out.

A console reported the head at 01:80:00 on a disc 01:28:48 long while
waiting for 00:02:16, with thirty-seven seeks against three waits and
twelve errors, and a boot slow enough to look hung. Every read was a
journey back from the rim.

Command 6 after each fill holds position rather than stopping the disc,
so the next read is a short seek from where the last one finished.
---
 bios/segacd.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/bios/segacd.c b/bios/segacd.c
index ec78d85..8990c76 100644
--- a/bios/segacd.c
+++ b/bios/segacd.c
@@ -1766,6 +1766,22 @@ static BOOL cd_fill(ULONG lba)
         memcpy(cd_cache[i], CDSECT, CDC_DATA_BYTES);
         cd_cache_have = (UBYTE)(i + 1);
     }
+
+    /* Hold the head where it is.
+     *
+     * Command 3 does not read a sector, it starts the drive reading and
+     * the drive keeps going. Between one read and the next -- across
+     * GEMDOS, across a whole request -- nothing was stopping it, so it
+     * ran forward to the end of the disc and sat in the lead-out. A
+     * console reported the head at 01:80:00 on a disc 01:28:48 long
+     * while waiting for 00:02:16, thirty-seven seeks against three
+     * waits, and a boot slow enough to look hung.
+     *
+     * Command 6 holds position rather than stopping the disc, so the
+     * next read is a short seek from where this one finished instead of
+     * a journey back from the rim. */
+    cdd_ask_ready();
+    cd_streaming = 0;
     return TRUE;
 }
 
